       <widget class="QLabel" name="patterns_frame_label">
        <property name="font">
         <font>
          <bold>true</bold>
         </font>
        </property>
        <property name="text">
         <string>Screenshot name patterns</string>
        </property>
       </widget>
      </item>
      <item>
       <widget class="ScreenshotNamePatternsEditor" name="patterns_editor">
        <property name="toolTip">
         <string>Each pattern is a regular expression matched against a filename's stem, case-insensitively. One capture group names the slot as a number; no capture group means slot 0. Double-click a cell to edit it.</string>
        </property>
       </widget>
      </item>
      <item>
       <widget class="WrappingLabel" name="patterns_order_label">
        <property name="text">
         <string>Order decides which pattern matches first when more than one could — an ordinary list, evaluated top to bottom — and which file takes a slot two names want. A pattern that fails to compile, or carries more than one capture group, is skipped and shown in red. An empty list falls back to the shipped patterns.</string>
        </property>
        <property name="wordWrap">
         <bool>true</bool>
        </property>
       </widget>
      </item>
     </layout>
    </widget>
   </item>
   <item>
    <widget class="QFrame" name="collisions_frame">
     <property name="frameShape">
      <enum>QFrame::Shape::StyledPanel</enum>
     </property>
     <property name="frameShadow">
      <enum>QFrame::Shadow::Raised</enum>
     </property>
     <layout class="QVBoxLayout" name="collisions_frame_layout">
      <item>
       <widget class="QLabel" name="collisions_frame_label">
        <property name="font">
         <font>
          <bold>true</bold>
         </font>
        </property>
        <property name="text">
         <string>Always applied</string>
        </property>
       </widget>
      </item>
      <item>
       <widget class="WrappingLabel" name="collisions_label">
        <property name="text">
         <string>Converting renames each image to the number its name already carries. When two names want the same number, the first pattern above wins it and the other image keeps its own name — nothing is renamed away and nothing is deleted. One name under several extensions is one picture: the largest by pixel size takes the number.</string>
        </property>
        <property name="toolTip">
         <string>These rules are not configurable — they apply whatever the patterns above say. An image left under its own name is corrected in the images dock, one file at a time.</string>
        </property>
        <property name="wordWrap">
         <bool>true</bool>
        </property>
       </widget>
      </item>
     </layout>
    </widget>
   </item>
